<article class="env-proposition" id="09NZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09NZ">Proposition <span data-tag="09NZ">33.38.12</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a Noetherian separated scheme of dimension $1$. Then $X$ has an ample invertible sheaf. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $Z \subset X$ be the reduction of $X$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/09NX" data-tag="09NX">33.38.10</a> the scheme $Z$ has an ample invertible sheaf. Thus by Lemma <a href="/tag/09NY" data-tag="09NY">33.38.11</a> there exists an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{L}$ on $X$ whose restriction to $Z$ is ample. Then $\mathcal{L}$ is ample by an application of Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/09MS" data-tag="09MS">30.17.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>